  "detailed_description": "[0033] Technical solutions in related art are not able to achieve satisfactory stabilization effects under complex scenes. For example, when a user takes a video while walking, related art technologies cannot effectively reduce the shaking caused by the movement of the user's body. This is because the existing technologies mainly rely on optical flow estimation to correct the shaking of the camera, but the optical flow estimation is easily affected by the scene changes, light changes, etc., resulting in poor robustness. Moreover, the existing technologies do not consider the relationship between the movements of different objects in the scene, so they cannot accurately determine whether the shaking is caused by the movement of the user or other factors.
