[0052] It can be understood that the foregoing solution of the present application can obtain the motion trajectory of the object through the fusion of the radar sensing data and the image, and then control the camera to move along the predicted motion trajectory to implement the Electronic Image Stabilization (EIS). Compared with the traditional EIS technology, the proposed solution can better adapt to the scenario where the camera moves rapidly, and significantly improves the anti-shake performance of the camera.
[0053] In addition, the proposed solution can also be used for EIS cropping. That is, the proposed solution can be used to determine whether the motion is global motion or local motion, and then adjust the cropping range accordingly.
[0054] Specifically, the proposed solution can determine whether the motion is global motion or local mo tion by analyzing the motion characteristics of the obje cts in the scene. If the motion of the object is inconsisten t with most other objects, it indicates that the motion is l oc al motion, and the cropping range needs to be adjusted accor dingly. Otherwise, if the motion of the object is consisten t with most other objects, it indicates that it is global motion, and no adjustment is required. By doing so, the proposed solution can ensure that the cropping range is accurate and effective, thereby improving the overall stabilization effect.
