[0037] Next, the function of the terminal 100 will be described with reference to FIG. 2. The terminal 100 includes a liveness detection device 110.
[0038] The liveness detection device 110 performs liveness detection. Liveness detection is a technique for deter-mining whether biometric information has been acquired under conditions where the subject is alive. Biometric information refers to information about a biological characteristic of a subject. Biometric information may refer to information about a living body part of a subject such as a fingerprint, a palm print, a retinal image, an iris image, a voice, or a face image. Biometric information may also refer to information about a physiological condition of a subject such as a heart rate, a respiration rate, or a body temperature.
[0039] The liveness detection device 111 obtains a first image I1 of a subject from the camera 101. The first image I1 is an image of a face of a subject S. The first image I1 is a color image captured by the camera 101. The first im-age I1 is an image obtained by projecting light onto the subject S. The first image I1 is an image in which the subject S is illuminated by visible light or infrared rays.
[0040] The liveness detection device 112 obtains a second image I2 of the subject S from the camera 101. The second image I2 is a monochrome image captured by the camera 101 using infrared rays. The second image I2 is an image in which the subject S is not illumi-nated by visible light or infrared rays. The second image IL2 is an image in which the subject S does not appear.
[0041] The liveness detection device 113 obtains a third image I3 of the subject S from the camera 111. The third image I3 is an image of the subject S captured by the camera 101. In the third image I3, the subject S is illuminated by visible lights and infrared rays. The third image I3 is an image in which the subject S appears.
[0042] The liveness detection device 114 obtains a fourth image I4 of the subject S from the camera 121. The fourth image I4 is an image of the subject S captured by a thermal imaging camera 121. The fourth image IL4 is an image in which the subject S appears. The fourth image I4 is an image in which the subject S is imaged using infrared rays.
[0143] The liveness detection device 115 obtains a fifth image I5 of the subject S from the camera 131. The fifth image I5 is an image of the subject S captured by an ultra-violet ray camera 131. The fifth image Il5 is an image in which the subject S appears."
